1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,200
Before a wildfire becomes a live emergency,
teams need somewhere to rehearse

2
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:10,000
the decisions that come first.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,800
Local knowledge lives in people.
Spatial evidence lives on maps.

4
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:24,000
And an AI assistant usually reasons somewhere else.
Every handoff loses context.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
PyroScan Incident Twin turns the browser
into one shared rehearsal table,

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
grounded in La Palma's public terrain and
a Copernicus-observed 2023 burn scar.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:49,500
WebMCP lets the page expose its real verbs directly to ChatGPT:
read, inspect, annotate, simulate, compare, and stage.

8
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:58,000
No separate server.
No brittle click script.

9
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:08,500
I ask at the level of intent. ChatGPT focuses El Paso
and adds a blocked-road exercise note for the LP-3 checkpoint.

10
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:20,000
That local constraint becomes visible to me—
and available to every later tool call.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Next, a sixty-minute northeast wind shift redraws
the deterministic attention area on the same map.

12
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:40,000
This is not a forecast; it is a bounded what-if
that a person and an agent can inspect together.

13
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:49,000
PyroScan compares two reversible response options
against setup time, coverage, resource use,

14
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:58,000
and the new access constraint. The ranking lives
on screen—not buried in a chat transcript.

15
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Before staging, ChatGPT reads the exact board version.
If the evidence changed, a stale plan is rejected.

16
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:20,000
The new draft carries the LP-3 constraint into its access action,
proving that human knowledge changed the downstream artifact.

17
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:27,000
The agent can explore.
It cannot approve.

18
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Final approval is deliberately absent from the WebMCP tools
and remains with the exercise director.

19
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:40,500
Synthetic. Deterministic. Browser-only. Open source.
No live feed, dispatch, or hidden backend.

20
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:48,000
The ambition: rehearse trade-offs before a crisis makes them irreversible.
PyroScan. Wildfire readiness, rehearsed together.
